                        "glosses": [
                            "An individual viewing of a web page by a user, often counted when measuring a web site's popularity."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Internet"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9dae8fe4-feef-44ac-bd47-11144a97eec8",
                                "sense_id": "a4e04ddc-fe42-395d-9774-b2cc6f4fefeb",
                                "text": "Similarly, Trueman, Wong, and Zhang found that the nonfinancial measures of unique visitors and pageviews provide additional explanatory power for stock prices, especially for e-tailers like Amazon.com."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1d3f1306-c489-41ef-8cd0-e0bb5c8d00f8",
                                "sense_id": "a4e04ddc-fe42-395d-9774-b2cc6f4fefeb",
                                "text": "And you—you clueless, literate shmuck—are but a pawn in this game. So just let go. Just accept the fact that you are reading this column right now simply because we can count you as a number on a spreadsheet. You are a pageview, my friend. You are a \"monthly unique visitor.\" One of millions. Nothing more, nothing less."
                            }
